NeoSCAD patch to wgpu-core 30.0.1 (crates.io): fix a spurious assertion
failure in Device::maintain when several threads poll the same device.

Upstream: https://github.com/gfx-rs/wgpu/pull/9958, merged to trunk as
commit 385520f72f5bbb614fec957ed31f3f6d19076a3f (2026-08-07). This is that
commit's wgpu-core/src/device/resource.rs change, applied unchanged (it
applies cleanly to 30.0.1), plus two "NeoSCAD patch" marker comments. The
commit's CHANGELOG.md entry is not part of the crate and is left out.

Apply from the pristine crate root: patch -p1 < this file.
See vendor/README.md ("wgpu-core 30.0.1, patched").

